    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>1. Public Advisory Portal</strong></td>
      <td>
        • Brand showcase &amp; corporate advisory positioning<br>
        • Interactive Sri Lankan VAT, Corporate Tax &amp; UAE FTA calculators<br>
        • Responsive service booking &amp; quote inquiry engine<br>
        • Insightful corporate knowledge hub &amp; blog CMS<br>
        • Colombo &amp; Global contact channels with verified SLA routing
      </td>
      <td>Prospective Clients, Global Partners, Investors</td>
      <td><span class="tag-done">&#10004; Complete</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>2. Client Self-Service Portal</strong></td>
      <td>
        • Personalized client command dashboard (`/portal/dashboard`)<br>
        • Multi-currency Expense Manager with cloud receipt upload<br>
        • Service inquiry tracker with real-time status updates<br>
        • Secure Document Hub for statutory filings, audits, and VAT returns<br>
        • Profile security, session review, and password rotation
      </td>
      <td>Retained Clients, SME Business Owners, Finance Directors</td>
      <td><span class="tag-done">&#10004; Complete</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>3. Double-Entry General Ledger (Accounts-Web)</strong></td>
      <td>
        • Standardized 5-bucket Chart of Accounts (Assets, Liab, Eq, Rev, Exp)<br>
        • Strict balanced-entry journal voucher verification (Debits = Credits)<br>
        • Real-time automated Trial Balance computation<br>
        • Instant Profit &amp; Loss (P&amp;L) financial statements generation<br>
        • Historical audit trail with immutable timestamped records
      </td>
      <td>Senior Accountants, Audit Managers, Finance Controllers</td>
      <td><span class="tag-done">&#10004; Complete</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>4. Executive Admin Control Suite</strong></td>
      <td>
        • Real-time business KPIs: Active accounts, users, expense backlog<br>
        • Contact message dispatcher with read/unread notifications<br>
        • Role-Based Access Control (Admin vs Client vs Staff)<br>
        • Integrated CMS for publishing client testimonials and insights<br>
        • Parallel SQL telemetry executing in sub-100ms response times
      </td>
      <td>Executive Board, Managing Director, Practice Partners</td>
      <td><span class="tag-done">&#10004; Complete</span></td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- ══════════════════ SECTION 3: FINANCIAL ANALYSIS & ROI ══════════════════ -->
<h1>3. Financial Return on Investment (ROI) &amp; Operational Economics</h1>
<p>
  A rigorous financial analysis demonstrates significant capital efficiency, reduced headcount drag, and increased client throughput made possible by the AccBots custom software infrastructure.
</p>

<h2>3.1 Operational Efficiency &amp; Labor Savings</h2>
<p>
  Historically, onboarding a new corporate client, gathering preliminary invoices, calculating tax liability, and producing monthly trial balance reconciliations required <strong>14.5 staff hours per client per month</strong>. Under the AccBots digital workflow:
</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 35%;">Operational Process</th>
      <th style="width: 20%;">Legacy Manual Process</th>
      <th style="width: 20%;">AccBots Automated System</th>
      <th style="width: 25%;">Efficiency Gain</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Client Onboarding &amp; Intake</td>
      <td>3.5 hours / client</td>
      <td>0.2 hours / client</td>
      <td><strong>94% Reduction</strong> (Self-service signup)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Expense Entry &amp; Receipt Filing</td>
      <td>4.0 hours / client</td>
      <td>0.5 hours / client</td>
      <td><strong>87% Reduction</strong> (Cloud attachment)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Tax Estimates &amp; Scenarios</td>
      <td>2.5 hours / inquiry</td>
      <td>0.0 hours / inquiry</td>
      <td><strong>100% Automated</strong> (Online calculators)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>General Ledger &amp; Trial Balance</td>
      <td>4.5 hours / period</td>
      <td>0.5 hours / period</td>
      <td><strong>89% Reduction</strong> (One-click generation)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Total Monthly Resource Per Client</strong></td>
      <td><strong>14.5 Hours</strong></td>
      <td><strong>1.2 Hours</strong></td>
      <td><strong>91.7% Overall Labor Reallocation</strong></td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>3.2 Infrastructure Unit Economics (Annual Cost Comparison)</h2>
<p>
  By choosing an open, modern architecture (Next.js + Supabase Postgres + Cloudflare R2 on Railway) rather than bloated legacy enterprise platforms (e.g. Salesforce + Auth0 + NetSuite), annual operational expenditures have been curtailed:
</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 40%;">Expense Category</th>
      <th style="width: 30%;">Legacy SaaS Equivalent (Annual)</th>
      <th style="width: 30%;">AccBots Cloud Infrastructure (Annual)</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Authentication / Identity Provider</td>
      <td>$4,200 (Auth0 / Okta Tier)</td>
      <td>$0 (Built-in custom JWT + Argon2/Bcrypt)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Cloud Hosting &amp; App Container</td>
      <td>$7,800 (Enterprise Cloud VM)</td>
      <td>$240 (Railway Standard Container Tier)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Relational Database Cluster</td>
      <td>$6,000 (Managed Enterprise DB)</td>
      <td>$300 (Supabase Postgres Production Tier)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Document &amp; Receipt Storage</td>
      <td>$1,800 (AWS S3 + Data Egress)</td>
      <td>$60 (Cloudflare R2 Zero-Egress Storage)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Total Annual Infrastructure Cost</strong></td>
      <td><strong>$19,800 / year</strong></td>
      <td><strong>$600 / year</strong></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="background-color: #FEF3C7;">
      <td colspan="2"><strong>Net Annual Infrastructure Savings for Board Allocation</strong></td>
      <td><strong style="color: #92400E;">$19,200 Savings / Year (97%)</strong></td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

